1
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:09,259
-[insects chirping]
-[rumbling]

2
00:00:12,011 --> 00:00:14,764
[dinosaurs bellowing]

3
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,248
[thudding]

4
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:46,463
[roars, screeches]

5
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,021
[grunts, pants]

6
00:01:04,063 --> 00:01:05,982
[fly buzzing]

7
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,905
[all panting]

8
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:16,284
[shudders, sighs]

9
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:21,706
Oh...

10
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:22,916
Okay...

11
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,086
-[screams]
-[all scream]

12
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,422
[sighs] Sorry, I stepped on a twig.

13
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:31,966
-Ugh, come on, man.
-You done gave me a heart attack!

14
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:34,260
-I should step on you.
-It's okay, Ben.

15
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:36,721
-We're all on edge.
-And lost.

16
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:39,015
Yeah, we've been out here for a while now.

17
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:41,893
Darius, we sure we're still headed
towards the park?

18
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,853
Well, we'd be sure
if I still had my phone,

19
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:47,774
because it has a GPS, a compass app,
and is also a phone!

20
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,276
Sammy didn't steal your phone!

21
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,820
No one stole your phone!

22
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:54,322
Can we please stop talking
about the phone?

23
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:57,033
You guys! You guys, you guys, you guys.

24
00:01:57,116 --> 00:01:59,786
Could you all yell at each other
quieter, please?

25
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:02,789
My fellow campers, chill!

26
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:07,794
What we need here is someone who can
make the hard call on what to do next.

27
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:10,130
Since I'm obviously leadership material...

28
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:12,715
I'll do this.

29
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,843
And my first decree as leader is

30
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:19,389
for everyone to stop talking
and just listen to Darius.

31
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:22,600
-Huh?
-You got us out of camp alive.

32
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:26,646
Plus, I can blame you
if anybody gets eaten.

33
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:27,897
Leadership. [chuckles]

34
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:30,233
So, which way, Darius?

35
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:39,534
Please, you're just trying to cover up
the fact that you're lost, too, Mr. VIP.

36
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,745
-None of us know where we are.
-I know where we are!

37
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:44,956
We're by the Carnotaurus paddock!

38
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:47,083
I thought this place looked familiar.

39
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:49,919
Am I an excellent leader or what?

40
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,465
I remember the fence.

41
00:02:55,758 --> 00:03:00,096
-The broken, ripped-down fence.
-[Ben panting]

42
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:04,601
That means... That means Toro
is out here... with us.

43
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:07,312
Now we have to deal
with the Indominus and Toro.

44
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:10,899
Hold up. How do you know about Toro?

45
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:14,193
We all know. Kenji told us, like,
the day after it happened.

46
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:18,239
In my defense,
me saving you was super cool.

47
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,365
[sighs]

48
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:21,868
We know this enclosure
is due north of the main park.

49
00:03:21,951 --> 00:03:24,996
So, if we keep going that way,
we'll hit the visitors' center.

50
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:28,416
We're sure to find Dave and Roxie,
or someone else there in charge.

51
00:03:28,499 --> 00:03:33,338
Yes! Exactly what I was thinking,
as leader, which I am.

52
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:35,089
Follow me!

53
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,762
I don't think finding an adult
is going to help.

54
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:44,098
A terrifying, camouflaged dinosaur
trashed our camp.

55
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:45,600
No way they have a plan for that.

56
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:49,062
Ben, I know it's scary,
but this is Jurassic World.

57
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,897
Dealing with dinosaurs is what they do.

58
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:54,442
They didn't deal so well
back at their first park, did they? Hmm?

59
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:57,278
Everything will be okay. Trust me.

60
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:07,288
[rumbling]

61
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:11,125
[growling]

62
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:15,129
[Roxie] Ugh! This is taking forever!

63
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:18,591
I know Claire's a busy lady,
but we can't leave the kids alone all day.

64
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:21,928
Wow, hittin' the first names.
You only do that when you're annoyed.

65
00:04:22,011 --> 00:04:23,680
Of course I'm annoyed, David.

66
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:26,182
We need to talk to Claire
and get back to the kids ASAP!

67
00:04:26,265 --> 00:04:28,643
But instead, they shove us in here
and just tell us to wait for her,

68
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:30,937
and then everyone just disappears!

69
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:33,314
Where'd they go?

70
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:35,358
Something's going on.

71
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:37,735
Look, I'm sure Claire--
yeah, that's not gonna work--

72
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:39,404
Ms. Dearing will get to us when she can.

73
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:43,408
When? We've been here so long,
someone gave you a birthday card to sign.

74
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:45,827
All right, the real issue
is that no one else signed it.

75
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:48,997
That's just sad. Poor... Eddie.

76
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,456
"Dear Eddie,

77
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,917
I don't know you,
but I'm sure you're doing..."

78
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:56,045
Will you put that down
and help me find a phone or radio?

79
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:59,465
We have to get ahold of someone,
ideally, Claire Dearing.

80
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,510
Okay, maybe she's hiding so she doesn't
have to sign this card and--

81
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:04,512
-Are you picking that lock?
-What?

82
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:06,472
I watched Brooklynn's
"Hacks for When You Lock Yourself

83
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:07,890
Out of Your Hotel Room" video.

84
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:10,393
It was actually so good, I subscribed.

85
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:11,728
Don't tell her.

86
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,939
-Almost.
-[lock clicks]

87
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,232
Ugh, I'm so good.

88
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:17,817
Mildly impressive.

89
00:05:18,776 --> 00:05:21,029
[screaming over radios]

90
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:23,156
-[man 1] Shoot her!
-[screaming continues]

91
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:24,240
Shoot her!

92
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:27,243
-[man 2] No! The order is to get--
-[man 3] Save Wu!

93
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,829
-Keep out of the way!
-[velociraptors screeching]

94
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,623
[static crackles]

95
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:36,044
[birds chirping]

96
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,007
[Sammy grunts]

97
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:47,430
Don't let Brooklynn upset you.
She's just being... Brooklynn.

98
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:58,649
Yaz, there's something I... [gasps]

99
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:01,444
[Sammy] The Indominus rex was here.

100
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:05,364
[Darius] Predators don't kill prey
and then just leave without feeding.

101
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:07,200
This... this isn't right.

102
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:08,493
-[low groaning]
-[all gasp]

103
00:06:10,995 --> 00:06:12,455
[all scream, pant]

104
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,500
[Ben screams, pants]

105
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,461
[whimpers]

106
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:20,463
[rustling]

107
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:28,012
-[snarls]
-[all scream]

108
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,765
[soft growling]

109
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:33,226
Bumpy!

110
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,437
[chuckles]

111
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,315
And drooly, and smelly.

112
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:41,359
How do you even know
that's the same dinosaur?

113
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,652
Her big head bump.

114
00:06:42,735 --> 00:06:46,280
Dr. Wu said she's asymmetrical,
but he's wrong that it's bad.

115
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:48,533
And so what if she is asymmetrical?

116
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:51,494
There's nothing wrong
with being different, or bumpy,

117
00:06:51,577 --> 00:06:54,664
or getting tired after reading
an overly thrilling book!

118
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:57,208
And maybe if her parents
had listened to her,

119
00:06:57,291 --> 00:07:00,044
she wouldn't have come here
and gotten attacked!

120
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,089
Are we still talking about the dinosaur?

121
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:05,299
Feels like we're not still talking
about the dinosaur.

122
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:09,804
As fun as this reunion is,
shouldn't we keep moving south?

123
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:12,515
I'm not spending another hour
walking through the jungle,

124
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:15,017
hoping that we don't
run into that Indominus.

125
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,477
We need a new plan.

126
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:20,022
Uh, yeah, obviously we need a new plan.

127
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:22,733
So, I had Darius figure out a new one.

128
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,235
Lay it on us, bro.

129
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:25,236
Okay.

130
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:30,241
So, uh... we need to find
somewhere safe close by.

131
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:33,619
If camp is that way,
and the park is that way...

132
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:36,873
[gasps] Isn't Dr. Wu's field genetics lab
near here?

133
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:39,417
You guys went on the tour.
Does this area look familiar?

134
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:42,670
Um... Yeah. Y-Yeah.

135
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,631
-I think it might be over that way.
-That seems right.

136
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,341
Great! That's where we should go.

137
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:50,761
There's bound to be an adult there
who can help or tell us what to do.

138
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:51,846
Right?

139
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:54,265
-[faint roaring]
-[all gasp]

140
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:56,809
Fine, whatever! Let's just go to the lab.

141
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:59,270
As long as we are moving away from that.

142
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:01,439
[soft growling]

143
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:02,523
What about Bumpy?

144
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,275
She's a dinosaur, bro.

145
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:06,027
She belongs out here in the wild.

146
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:08,613
And she'll just slow us down.
We gotta go now.

147
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:11,157
[soft growling]

148
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,508
Ugh! [grunts]

149
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:31,719
We're doing the right thing, yeah?
Going towards the genetics lab?

150
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:34,847
Or should we have stayed at camp?
Would that have been safer?

151
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:36,557
How are you so calm about this?

152
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:41,270
I told you, if someone gets eaten,
I'm not to blame, you are.

153
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:43,147
Lea-der-ship.

154
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:47,693
But if I'm leading us the wrong way,
the person getting eaten could be you.

155
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:50,238
Are you sure
we should be going to the lab?

156
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:51,239
[screams]

157
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:52,907
Why are we moving so slowly?

158
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,742
Let's pick it up, people.

159
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:57,119
Wait.

160
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,454
Guys, where's Ben?

161
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,707
[grunting]

162
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:04,627
-[soft growling]
-Shh! Shh!

163
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:06,671
-Come on. Oh!
-[Yasmina clears throat]

164
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:09,048
Hey!

165
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:12,426
How's it hangin'... dudes?

166
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:15,137
Ben, are you hiding Bumpy in that bush?

167
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:17,348
[soft bellowing]

168
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:19,725
Nope. That could be anything.

169
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,978
The jungle makes
all sorts of weird noises.

170
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:24,188
-[soft growling]
-[grunts]

171
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,441
How did she get here?

172
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:28,901
We don't have time for this!

173
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:32,238
There are dinosaurs eating people
out here, and Bumpy can't keep up!

174
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:33,781
She can move faster.

175
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:36,659
Ankylosauruses run fast. Right, Darius?

176
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:39,912
When they're fully grown, maybe,
but she's just...

177
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:42,999
[snoring]

178
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:46,294
Wow! Yeah, total speed demon.

179
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:47,712
Say goodbye, Ben.

180
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,839
[groans]

181
00:09:54,885 --> 00:09:55,928
No!

182
00:09:56,762 --> 00:10:00,308
You say hello,
because she is coming with us!

183
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,101
So... there!

184
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:05,771
Ben, you're not thinking this through.
Bumpy's too slow.

185
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:10,192
Then... then we'll put her in the van!

186
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,485
[scoffs] What van?

187
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:12,945
That one!

188
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:20,786
It's an ACU transport!

189
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:22,413
Asset containment unit.

190
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:23,831
Got the tour of their HQ.

191
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:27,376
Super hardcore dino-trapping
security dudes.

192
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,919
Then where are they?

193
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,465
-Is that a tablet? [grunts]
-[Darius grunts]

194
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:37,261
[sighs] What did they tell us?

195
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:40,139
Oh, right. Come on, channel six.

196
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:42,683
Dave, Roxie! Can y'all hear us?

197
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,810
[static crackles]

198
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:49,357
And of course this doesn't have
communication enabled.

199
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,525
Because you know what?
Why would it?

200
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:52,860
If I had my phone--

201
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:54,612
Enough already!

202
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:57,365
There are bigger things
going on here than your phone!

203
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:00,743
[tablet beeping]

204
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:05,581
There's a map program
with little moving dots on it.

205
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:08,250
[Darius] They chip all the dinosaurs
electronically to track them.

206
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,461
See? There's us, and there's...

207
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:15,716
Wait. Here's the Brachiosaurus Grove
on the map,

208
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,469
so why are the Brachiosauruses
way over there?

209
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:21,889
I think maybe the fences are down.

210
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:24,141
-At least some of them.
-[Bumpy growls]

211
00:11:24,308 --> 00:11:27,395
[squealing]

212
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:30,106
[pants] Easy, girl.

213
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:33,692
[rumbling]

214
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,654
-[Bumpy whines]
-[Ben] Guys?

215
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:38,739
Something's coming this way.

216
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,199
That's weird.

217
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:43,202
Whatever that is,
it isn't showing up on the tablet.

218
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:45,746
What kind of dinosaur
wouldn't have a transponder?

219
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:48,290
I am not in the mood to find out.

220
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:50,626
-[Bumpy squealing]
-[Ben] Shh! Shh!

221
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:55,714
-Ben, shut her up!
-[roaring]

222
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,466
[screams] We gotta go now!

223
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,218
-[Brooklynn] Go! Go!
-[Darius] Move!

224
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:06,517
Wait! Doesn't anyone know
how to drive a van?

225
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,770
No, but we drove gyrospheres, right?

226
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,021
It can't be that different.

227
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:13,983
The gyrospheres had joysticks
and a Jimmy Fallon tutorial.

228
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:16,193
-I don't even have my learners permit!
-I do!

229
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:17,486
[grunts]

230
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,781
-Hands at ten and two--
-Kenji, go, quickly!

231
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,658
-[tires screech]
-[all scream]

232
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:24,201
[Ben] Wrong way! Wrong way!

233
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,495
-[Kenji grunts]
-[tires screech]

234
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:29,206
[roaring]

235
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:32,710
[roars]

236
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,129
It's gaining! Go faster!

237
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,881
-I can't!
-You're in the wrong gear!

238
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:39,300
-Well, how do I shift gears?
-How should I know?

239
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,718
[bellowing]

240
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:42,470
[all scream]

241
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:44,722
[roars]

242
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,516
-It's coming!
-Step on that thing!

243
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,852
-Zigzag!
-Are you signaling?

244
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:52,563
Can everyone not yell at me
while I'm saving our lives?

245
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:55,107
[roars]

246
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:56,859
Drive!

247
00:12:57,651 --> 00:13:00,571
[all screaming]

248
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:07,745
[Brooklynn] No!

249
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:11,790
[roars]

250
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:16,128
[all scream]

251
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:23,385
[all grunt, pant]

252
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,807
At least we lost Indominus.

253
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:32,686
-Now... where do we go?
-[Bumpy groans]

254
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:35,189
How about into the genetics lab?

255
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:40,110
It's a gift.

256
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:42,780
[doors hiss]

257
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:48,869
What?

258
00:13:52,831 --> 00:13:54,083
-[grunts]
-[all scream]

259
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:57,211
[screaming]

260
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:01,215
[sighs] Not dinosaurs.
You're not dinosaurs.

261
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:03,884
[sighs] This is the worst birthday ever.

262
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:11,517
Again, we are so happy we found you.
Things are crazy!

263
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,061
There's a giant camouflaged dinosaur
out there.

264
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:17,898
Also, regular dinosaurs.
We've been hoping to find someone--

265
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,150
You're sure you closed the door
behind you, right?

266
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:21,735
Uh...

267
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,404
I think so.

268
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:26,407
-You think, or you know?
-[Kenji belches]

269
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:28,659
Sorry?

270
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:30,953
Did you want it back?

271
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:32,872
You know what? Doesn't matter.

272
00:14:33,247 --> 00:14:36,500
The dinosaurs got out and no one
bothered to tell me; they just ran.

273
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:39,211
So, why not? Knock yourself out.

274
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:43,257
Ugh! There's no dial tone!

275
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:44,967
The landlines are down.

276
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,970
So is the radio, and cell phone service
keeps cutting out.

277
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:52,266
But the park obviously has a plan.

278
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:55,269
So, what's that plan? What do we do?

279
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:59,273
You're asking me? [laughs]

280
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,191
Asking me?

281
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,696
Is that, like, a good freaky laugh?

282
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:08,657
Do you not get it? We're doomed.

283
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,826
No one is coming to help!

284
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:14,121
But what about Dr. Wu, or--

285
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,707
Wu? Who do you think is to blame?

286
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:17,833
Wu got greedy.

287
00:15:17,916 --> 00:15:21,045
And instead of dinosaurs,
he built monsters!

288
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,963
[whirring]

289
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,429
Masrani, Dearing,

290
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:33,766
they're all clueless
about what's really going on here.

291
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:35,976
And after everything I did
for the other guys--

292
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:38,103
Other guys? What other--

293
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,480
It doesn't matter, does it?

294
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:41,732
Jurassic World isn't a park.

295
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:46,278
It's a powder keg,
and it is detonating all around us!

296
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,530
We're all going down.

297
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:49,990
End of story!

298
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,534
No, you have to know what to do.

299
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:53,953
You're an adult!

300
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:55,663
Don't look at me.

301
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:58,165
I was just hiding until you all barged in.

302
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,334
But we drove all the way here 'cause--

303
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:01,543
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

304
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:04,421
-You have a vehicle?
-[grunts]

305
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:08,300
Guys, I left the keys in the van.

306
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:14,139
Stop! What are you doing?

307
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:17,059
Getting out of here alive!

308
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,894
[panting]

309
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:20,896
-[grunts]
-[squeals]

310
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:22,314
[grunts]

311
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,232
Ow!

312
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:24,358
[squeals]

313
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:25,943
Bumpy! [pants]

314
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:28,404
-Huh? [pants]
-[engine starts]

315
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:30,531
-[engine revs]
-[Yasmina yelps]

316
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,455
[grunts]

317
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,376
-[roars]
-[all scream]

318
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:48,132
[roars]

319
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:55,305
[pants] Ah! [grunts]

320
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,683
-[growls]
-[yelps]

321
00:16:58,350 --> 00:16:59,643
[screams]

322
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,854
Oh, no! [whimpers]

323
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:05,607
[screams, whimpers]

324
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,652
-[pants]
-[metal creaks]

325
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:15,784
-[roars]
-[Eddie screams]

326
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:19,538
-[Sammy whimpers]
-[all panting]

327
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,586
-[Kenji] What?
-[Darius] Come on, are you kidding me?

328
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:29,256
Perfect! The park's only intact fence!

329
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:33,343
-[roaring]
-[all scream, pant]

330
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:38,265
I told you she'd get in the way!

331
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:40,768
If it wasn't for her,
I could have made the van.

332
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,438
And then you would have been eaten.
Bumpy saved your life.

333
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:46,482
Why couldn't you just leave her behind?

334
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:49,485
Because I won't abandon her like we were!

335
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,487
[low groaning]

336
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:55,866
Ben's right.

337
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:57,951
We're on our own.

338
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:01,538
-[roaring]
-[all scream]

339
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,373
[rumbling]

340
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,292
[panting]

341
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:10,005
[snarling]

342
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:18,931
[squeals]

343
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:22,643
-[Ben gasps]
-[Bumpy growls]

344
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:23,977
[snarls]

345
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:25,938
[shushing]

346
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,746
[growling]

347
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:49,628
[gasps]

348
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:55,217
[whispers] Trust me.

349
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,907
[roars]

350
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:33,881
[growling]

351
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:41,305
[clanging]

352
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:43,390
[roars]

353
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:49,396
[Ben and Kenji panting]

354
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:04,995
-[grunts, gasps]
-[tablet trilling]

355
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:06,997
-[roars]
-[whimpers]

356
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,750
-[all scream]
-Brooklynn!

357
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:12,544
[whimpers]

358
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,882
-[both scream]
-[snarls]

359
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:19,843
[both yelp]

360
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:23,722
-[screaming, panting]
-[rhythmic clanging]

361
00:20:25,974 --> 00:20:27,851
Hey, over here!

362
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,729
[roars]

363
00:20:32,981 --> 00:20:34,775
-[Darius] Whoa! [pants]
-[roars]

364
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:37,903
-[Sammy whimpering]
-[Bumpy squeals]

365
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:40,614
I'm driving.

366
00:20:41,114 --> 00:20:42,241
[engine starts]

367
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:45,118
Wait! Where's Darius?

368
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:48,038
-[roaring]
-[panting, whimpering]

369
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:49,456
Whoa!

370
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:53,919
-[screams]
-[snarling]

371
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,755
[panting]

372
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:00,467
[Darius yelps]

373
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:07,724
[roaring]

374
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:12,271
Whew! [pants, chuckles]

375
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:16,066
-[all laughing]
-[Bumpy squeals]

376
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,109
Yeah!

377
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,235
[Roxie over radio] Kids?

378
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:19,653
Come on, pick up!

379
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,947
There's something going on.
Stay at camp.

380
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:23,782
-We're heading to you.
-[static crackles]

381
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:25,867
[Darius] No, we're heading to you!

382
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:27,703
Darius! Wait, why are you--

383
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:29,288
We're fine, but we had to leave camp.

384
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,455
-What?
-What?

385
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,456
Long story.

386
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,625
[Yasmina] Short story:
a dinosaur ate camp.

387
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:37,629
[Kenji] Shorter story: epic leader Kenji
somehow got everyone out safely.

388
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:40,007
[Ben] And then we found a van and Bumpy!

389
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:42,134
[Bumpy squeals]

390
00:21:43,468 --> 00:21:44,303
I got nothing.

391
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:46,930
[Darius] We're cutting through the jungle
and heading to the main park.

392
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:50,350
Should be there soon.

393
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:52,769
-We're getting out of here!
-[cheering]

394
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:56,440
-Yeah! You hear that, Bumpy?
-Whoo! Driver en route.

395
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:57,733
[Kenji sighs]

396
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:00,736
Good job not getting me eaten, bro.

397
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:03,322
Thanks, "brah."

398
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:05,907
Oh, no, you-- you made that sound weird.

399
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,617
No more bro-talk for you.

400
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:21,923
[laughs]

401
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,383
We did it, camp family!

402
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,052
-And not a moment too--
-[all grunt]

403
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:27,137
[grunting continues]

404
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:32,225
[Brooklynn] My phone.

405
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,853
I knew it!

406
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:37,564
-[gasps]
-[Yasmina] Huh?

407
00:22:38,774 --> 00:22:39,775
Sammy?

408
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,569
-[crashing]
-[all screaming]

409
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:45,781
[theme music playing]

